{
  "_comment": [
    "Model registry. scripts/model_registry.py resolves a key + detected hardware into",
    "a concrete launch config and VALIDATES it (tp*pp*cp*dp == gpus, tp within a node,",
    "max_tokens_per_gpu*cp >= max_seq_len).",
    "",
    "Verified facts behind these entries (measured 2026-08-18):",
    "  - The tokenizer is BYTE-IDENTICAL across all five Qwen3.5 models",
    "    (sha256 4b565170da5bed0e), so ONE dataset serves all of them. No re-tokenization.",
    "  - The TRAINING chat-template render is byte-identical too, so",
    "    --loss-mask-type qwen3_5 and the published cap10/cap8 datasets are valid",
    "    unchanged for every entry here.",
    "  - Qwen3.5-0.8B's chat template differs from the rest in ONE way: it defaults",
    "    thinking OFF, so its *generation* prompt already closes the think block",
    "    ('<think>\\n\\n</think>\\n\\n') while 4B/9B/27B/35B end at '<think>\\n'. Training",
    "    targets start with '\\n</think>\\n\\n', which lines up with the latter. Hence",
    "    serve_enable_thinking=true for 0.8B only -- otherwise the block is doubled at",
    "    serving time and eval silently degrades.",
    "  - Param counts are from each repo's safetensors index total_size / 2 (bf16)."
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "max_seq_len": 32768,
    "global_batch_size": 128,
    "num_epoch": 1,
    "lr": "3e-6",
    "min_lr": "3e-7",
    "lr_warmup_fraction": 0.03,
    "serve_context_length": 65536
  },
  "models": {
    "qwen3.5-0.8b": {
      "hf_repo": "Qwen/Qwen3.5-0.8B",
      "slime_spec": "qwen3.5-0.8B.sh",
